* Migration Testing Plan

Interactive REPL-based test strategy for validating schema migration changes
incrementally during development and comprehensively before release. All code
is intended to live in =genegraph.user= or a new =genegraph.migration-test= namespace.

** Design Principles

- Tests run against real transformed events, not mocks
- Incremental: run a small, curated sample while making changes; switch to full
  corpus for release validation
- Results surface as concise summary maps suitable for =tap>= / Portal inspection
- Each schema cleanup fix maps to at least one specific assertion
- The same test functions work at both scales by taking a sequence of events

** Sample Corpus

A curated set of GDM UUIDs covering the required dimensions. Load these once
and reuse across all test runs.

*** Required Coverage Dimensions

| Dimension          | Values to cover                                                    |
|--------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| SOP version        | 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11                                             |
| Mode of Inheritance | AD, AR, X-Linked, Semidominant                                    |
| Evidence types     | null variant, de novo, other variant (AD); AR; segregation;        |
|                    | case-control; biochemical function; protein interaction;           |
|                    | expression; functional alteration (patient/non-patient);           |
|                    | model systems (non-human, cell culture); rescue (human,            |
|                    | non-human, cell culture, patient)                                  |
| Versioning         | ≥1 GDM with 3+ published versions (major and minor increments)     |
| Publish/unpublish  | ≥1 GDM with an unpublish event in its history                      |

